  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">East-South Africa Agriculture Forum</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The East - South Africa Agricultural Business &amp; Policy Forum, as well as a Speaking Day, will be organised in the Netherlands at the initiative of Agricultural Counsellors from the East and South African regions, namely Addis Ababa, Kampala, Nairobi, and Pretoria. The goal is to create a platform to discuss sustainable business and policy themes, including contributing to agrologistics systems, creating sustainable potato and dairy value chains, and sourcing protein transition to optimise feed production.The project aims to inform beneficiaries about developments, opportunities, local needs, events, and challenges. The Speaking Day offers companies a possibility for face-to-face meetings with individual Agricultural Counsellors in a regional setting.The project will focus on sustainable agribusiness initiatives aligned with the interests of Dutch and local private stakeholders. The project&apos;s goal is to create jobs, produce healthy food, and promote Dutch technologies and innovations in climate-smart and sustainable agriculture.</narrative>
  </description>
